    <h2>Personal Data Policy</h2>

    <p>
        The names, email addresses and other personal data entered on this journal
        website will be used exclusively for the purposes of the journal and will not
        be made available for any other purpose or to any other party, except as
        provided for by the applicable legislation of the Russian Federation.
    </p>

    <p>
        <a class="external-policy-link"
           href="https://english.spbu.ru/about/documents/policy-federal-state-budgetary-educational-institution-higher-education-st">
            Policy of the Federal State Budgetary Educational Institution of Higher
            Education 'St. Petersburg State University' regarding the Processing of
            Personal Data
        </a>
    </p>


    <h2>Consent to the Processing of Personal Data</h2>

    <p>
        By this action, I, hereinafter referred to as the 'Data Subject', in compliance
        with the requirements of Federal Law No. 152-FZ of 27 July 2006 'On Personal
        Data', hereby give my consent to the Personal Data Operator (SPbU) to process
        my personal data provided by completing the web form on the SPbU website at
        https://diffjournal.spbu.ru (hereinafter referred to as the 'Website'),
        submitted (completed) using the Website, including information provided by
        completing a web form on the Website.
    </p>

    <p>
        By 'processing of personal data', I understand the collection, recording,
        systematisation, accumulation, storage, updating, modification, use, transfer,
        anonymisation, blocking, deletion, destruction, indefinite retention, and any
        other actions (operations) with personal data performed by the Personal Data
        Operator as provided for by the applicable legislation of the Russian
        Federation.
    </p>

    <p>
        The processing of the Data Subject's personal data is carried out for the
        purposes of sending information messages regarding SPbU, providing advisory
        support by authorised SPbU staff, responding to enquiries submitted via the
        web form on the Website, and for other purposes provided for by the applicable
        legislation of the Russian Federation.
    </p>

    <p>
        The processing of the Data Subject's personal data may be carried out using
        automation tools and/or without the use of automation tools in accordance
        with the applicable legislation of the Russian Federation.
    </p>

    <p>
        SPbU takes the necessary legal, organisational and technical measures, or
        ensures that such measures are taken, to protect personal data from unlawful
        or accidental access, destruction, alteration, blocking, copying, provision,
        distribution, and from other unlawful actions in relation to personal data,
        and also undertakes to maintain the confidentiality of the Data Subject's
        personal data.
    </p>

    <p>
        This consent to the processing of my personal data provided by completing
        the web form on the Website, submitted (completed) using the Website, is
        effective from the moment the web form is submitted on the Website until
        the purposes of the processing are achieved or until the consent is withdrawn.
    </p>

    <p>
        The consent may be withdrawn by me on the basis of a written application sent
        to the Personal Data Operator.
    </p>


    <h2>Consent to the Processing of Personal Data Collected via Metric Programmes</h2>

    <p>
        By continuing to use the website https://diffjournal.spbu.ru (hereinafter referred to as the
        ''Website'') and clicking the ''Accept'' or ''Agree'' button on the Website, I, hereinafter referred
